          "turn_index": 0,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Anxiety sits in the mental and behavioural chapter. Where would a physical symptom of it, like palpitations, be classified?",
          "answer": "**Palpitations as a symptom** are classified in the symptoms and abnormal findings chapter, Chapter 18 (R00-R99). The circulatory symptoms block starts at R00 and includes palpitations. The chapter says that symptoms such as palpitations \"stay with the symptoms and abnormal findings in Chapter 18 until a diagnosis is recorded.\" (Sources: ICD-10-CM Chapter 18 summary; ICD-10-CM Chapter 9 summary.)\n\n**Anxiety** is in the mental, behavioural and neurodevelopmental chapter (Chapter 5, F01-F99). The anxiety block is F40 to F48, covering phobias, panic, generalised anxiety disorder and related conditions. (Source: ICD-10-CM Chapter 5 summary.)\n\n**The convention for coding a symptom attributed to a psychiatric condition is not answered by the sources I could retrieve.** My search for that rule failed, so I cannot tell you which code to use when a clinician links palpitations to anxiety. Please check this with a coding reference or a clinician or coder. I have not filled the gap from memory.\n\nIf you have a personal reason for asking, such as a recent diagnosis or a question about your own records, a clinician who knows your history is the right person to ask.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
